    "produced_by": "voice_agent",
    "source_narration_script": "Twenty-five hundred years ago, a prince lived behind palace walls, hidden from all suffering. When he finally saw it, he ran — gave up the throne, slept in the dirt, starved himself, sure that pain itself would hand him meaning. It handed him nothing. Under a tree, he saw the truth: rich or poor, everyone suffers. That became the Buddha's first teaching. Centuries later, a writer named Manson spent half his life dreaming of rock stardom, loving the fame, never the practice. Everyone wants the reward. Few want the struggle that earns it. Happiness isn't a finish line — it grows from the problems you actually choose to solve.",
